    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0733" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-08T14:00:00-05:00">October 8, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Department’s confidential instruction, No. 337, September 25. The Department
                    desires you to make no further statement which might appear to commit this
                    Government to any action in accordance with any of the provisions of the Central
                    American General Treaty of Peace and Amity of 1923,<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d647-f1"/> or which might be intended to imply the possibility of
                    any such action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d647-f1" n="42" xml:id="d647-f1-content">
                <p>Signed February 7, 1923, <hi rendition="#italic">Conference on Central American
                        Affairs</hi>, p. 287.</p>
            </note>
